  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 300 PM Monday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Mostly dry, with more-seasonable (less hot) \ntemperatures and low humidity levels that will trend higher by this \nweekend\n\nAn anomalously strong mid/upr-level ridge will build ewd and across \nthe TN Valley and srn Appalachians, with +2.5 to 3 standardized \nheight anomalies in the 850 to 200mb layer and 500 mb heights near \n600 dam by Wed, then weaken while retrograding into the lwr MS \nValley by early this weekend. \n\nDownstream of the ridging aloft, surface high pressure will extend \nacross NC through Thu, then drift offshore while weakening Fri into \nthe weekend. The related sensible weather will be dry, with more-\nseasonable (less hot) temperatures and low humidity levels that will \ntrend higher by this weekend. While some scattered convection will \nbe possible in a warming/moistening and destabilizing airmass by \nthis weekend, especially Sun, the relative best chance of rain will \naccompany the next frontal passage whose timing is generally favored \nearly next week.",
